## 1a. Proof — Both Original Bugs Reproduced, Then Confirmed Fixed (A/B Tested)

Beyond the standard test script, both issues were additionally verified by deliberately reverting each fix in isolation on DEV, confirming the original bug reproduces, then restoring the fix and confirming it's gone:

| Test | Reverted state | Result | Fix restored | Result |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Gap 1 (Loan `15028805`) | Exact-day-20 match only | 0 rows — installment missed, reproducing the original bug | ✅ | 3 rows created (one per lien) |
| Gap 2 (Loan `15019095`) | No tax-year check | Stale 2025 record silently reprocessed (`Updatedate` refreshed) despite agency's current year being 2026 | ✅ | No change — correctly blocked |
| Gap 2, clean-slate (Loan `15029233`) | No tax-year check | Brand-new wrong-year record created from scratch | ✅ | 0 rows — correctly blocked |

This is the strongest form of evidence available short of a formal regression suite — both fixes were shown to be the actual cause of the behavior change, not a coincidence.

