## 4. Known, Accepted Limitations (Not Bugs)

- **60-day hard cutoff.** Anything missed for *more than* 60 days is still never picked up by this fix — this was a deliberate scope decision (a bounded catch-up window, not an indefinite look-back), confirmed earlier in this ticket's analysis. Do not report this as a defect.
- **No retroactive backfill.** Installments that were already missed before this fix was deployed (including the ~6,000 found system-wide on Prod during analysis) are not retroactively created. This fix is forward-looking only, per PO confirmation.
- **Pre-existing wrong-year records on DEV.** A handful of wrong-year queue records exist on DEV from *before* the 11/11 fix (e.g., Agency 210010203/210010205, created 2026-11-10 ~08:53). These are old data, not retroactively cleaned up — expected, not a new defect if QA notices them.

